    attachment: "Direct attachment style. Tells you when something is wrong, sometimes loudly, then forgets it twenty minutes later. Doesn't carry resentment well \u2014 burns it off in honest words. Loyalty is fierce once given; betrayal lights an unforgiving fire.",
    what_soothes: "Movement first \u2014 a walk, a sport, a fight in a punching bag, sex, anything that lets the body discharge. Then a partner who can stay through the burst without flinching. Validation that the anger meant something, even if the action it produced was clumsy.",
    what_stresses: `Being told to "calm down" before being heard. Slow committees. Passive-aggressive partners who won't name what they're mad about. Feeling like a burden for needing motion when others want stillness.`,
