    one_liner: "The thorn, the giant, the protective force with edges \u2014 what hurts to touch but keeps you safe.",
    meaning: `Thurisaz means "giant" or "thorn." It is the rune of Thor's hammer, the rune of the thorn-hedge that protects the rose and pierces the careless hand. Thurisaz is *defensive force* \u2014 the gate, the boundary, the saint's sword. It is also the rune of obstacle, the moment when the world says NO so that something better can later say yes. It is the most contested rune in modern reading because it is double-faced: the same force that wounds you is the force that protects you.`,
    upright: "Protection, boundary, a difficult test that strengthens, the force of the cosmos clearing what cannot stand. Conflict that resolves cleanly. A no that is a kindness. Thor strikes the giant; the road opens.",
