    meaning: "The ankh is the oldest symbol of life on earth that we still know how to read. Pharaohs carry it, gods extend it, mummies clutch it. The loop is the eternal \u2014 the sun rising again, the breath returning to the body, the soul finding its way back through. The cross beneath is the body, the manifest, the river you are walking. Together: the eternal married to the temporary, the soul embodied. To wear an ankh is not to ward off death but to remember that death is not the opposite of life \u2014 only of the body. Life itself, like the loop, has no opposite.",
