    meaning: "The lotus is held sacred in every major eastern tradition: in Egypt as the bloom from which Ra was born, in India as the seat of Lakshmi and the throne of the Buddha, in China and Japan as the symbol of purity. What every tradition agrees on is the *mud*. The lotus does not grow despite the swamp; it grows *because* of the swamp. Its roots are sunk in dark, fermenting, decaying matter \u2014 and the flower above is luminous, hydrophobic, untouched. The water beads off it. To pull a lotus and wash its petals is unnecessary; the flower has been doing its own washing while you slept. The teaching is exact: the conditions you grew in are not the conditions of the flower.",
