    slug: "fish",
    text: "Fish Pose",
    translation: "Matsyasana. Matsya = fish, asana = posture. The pose attributed to Matsya, the first incarnation of Vishnu.",
    tradition: "Hatha Yoga \u2014 named in the Gheranda Samhita (ch. 2 v. 21); traditionally practiced as the counter-pose to shoulderstand",
