    <p><strong>One root, four branches.</strong> Patanjali names avidya \u2014 ignorance, the seeing of the impermanent as permanent \u2014 as the field (<em>kshetra</em>) from which the other four kleshas grow as crops. Soften avidya and all five soften together.</p>
