    in_love: "Bastet in love is the partner who *makes the household feel like the safest-and-warmest place in the world* \u2014 whose presence is the cat-on-the-bed, the perfume-in-the-air, the music-in-the-kitchen, the laughter-of-the-children. Bastet-energy in a partnership is *the domestic-joy-as-sacred-register* \u2014 the recognition that the home is not the boring-counterpart to the exciting-elsewhere, but is itself the *Bubastis-festival ground* where the living happens. The shadow is the partner whose Bastet has *gone to Sekhmet* (the fierce-sister-aspect) and stayed there \u2014 the protective-mother-of-the-household whose protectiveness has become rage-at-any-perceived-threat-to-the-children. The other shadow: the partner whose Bastet has been *exiled* (the no-cats, no-perfume, no-music, no-festival household) \u2014 and the slow-domestic-decay that follows when the goddess is not in residence.",
    in_work: "Bastet in work is the *hospitality-host* (the figure who makes the workplace feel like a home, who tends the small-warmth-rituals that make people want to stay); the *defender-of-the-team* (the manager whose Bastet-protection actually-shields the team from the political-storms above); the *perfumer-and-aesthete* (the design-lead, the sensory-experience-designer, anyone whose work is *making spaces pleasant*); the *pet-friendly-workplace-creator* (the literal-Bastet \u2014 the leader who institutes the cat-friendly-office, the dog-friendly-policy, the recognition that animal-presence improves human-work). Bastet-energy is *domestic-joy-as-organizational-principle*. The shadow is the workplace whose Bastet has been *exiled* (the sterile-corporate, the no-pets-no-plants-no-music ethos) \u2014 and the productivity-collapse-by-soul-attrition that follows. The other shadow: the workplace whose Bastet has *gone to Sekhmet* (the protective-mother-figure who has become the fierce-defender against any criticism of her team, refusing all external feedback as attack).",
    the_gift: "Bastet gives the recognition that *domestic-joy is sacred*. The cat-on-the-bed, the perfume-in-the-air, the music-in-the-kitchen, the laughter-of-the-children, the Bubastis-festival of *seven-hundred-thousand-pilgrims-coming-to-celebrate-with-music-and-dance-and-drink* \u2014 these are not the trivial-decorations of life, they are the *liturgy of Bastet*. The gift is the willingness to *make the household into Bubastis* \u2014 to host the small-daily-festival, to be the one in the room who tends the milk-for-the-cat and the perfume-in-the-bath and the music-in-the-kitchen. And \u2014 through the eye-of-Ra register \u2014 the recognition that *the gentle-protector is the same goddess as the fierce-protector*, and that calling Bastet does not exclude having Sekhmet on standby for the moments when the household-threshold is actually breached.",
