  const title = "The 12 Persian / Zoroastrian Yazatas \u2014 Ahura Mazda, the six Amesha Spentas, and the great Yazatas \xB7 gab44 \u2728";
  const description = "Hand-written guides to the 12 canonical Persian / Zoroastrian divine-beings \u2014 Ahura Mazda the Wise Lord, the six Amesha Spentas (Vohu Manah / Asha Vahishta / Khshathra Vairya / Spenta Armaiti / Haurvatat / Ameretat), and the great Yazatas (Anahita / Mithra / Sraosha / Verethragna / Atar). Three families \u2014 Ahura Mazda & the Cosmic Triad, Earth-Waters-Plants-Royal-Waters, Covenant-Obedience-Victory-Fire \u2014 paired with zodiac sign, planet, and chakra. Source-honest from the Gathas of Zarathustra, the Yasna, the 21 Yashts (including the long Mihr-Yasht and Aban-Yasht), the Vendidad, the Bundahishn, the Denkard \u2014 and modern Mary Boyce, Albert de Jong, Almut Hintze, Prods Oktor Skj\xE6rv\xF8 scholarship. The first ethical monotheism in human religious history (c. 1200-1000 BCE on the Gathic linguistic dating), foundational to Abrahamic dualism (Satan / angels / messiah / end-times / soul-judgment / bodily-resurrection / heaven-and-hell all canonically downstream of Zoroastrian Ahriman / Yazatas / Saoshyant / Chinvat-Bridge / Frashokereti). Honest about the 651 CE Arab conquest, the contemporary ~25,000 Iranian Zoroastrians and ~60,000 Parsi diaspora demographic crisis, the Roman Mithras-cult appropriation, Nietzsche's Zarathustra cipher, the Faravahar nationalist-tattoo decontextualization, the Yazidi-confusion, the Bah\xE1'\xED-confusion, the fire-worshipper misreading.";
